  <UserdefinedSymbols/>
  <Comments>In this game,

1. Most numbers are x*10^5 in 4 bytes or 8 bytes. If x is the number shown on screen.
2. Percentages are x*10^3 in 4 bytes or 8 bytes. If x% is the number shown on screen.
3. Apart from that all other numbers are either exactly same in memory as they are on screen or they are between their extremes.

If a number cannot be found using 1,2,3, then assume that the number shown on screen is approximate.
For eg. if 55 is shown in screen, then it might be a value between 55*10^5 and 56*10^5.

The devs have made sure that the gpu never serves as bottleneck while playing. Most workloads are CPU bound.</Comments>
</CheatTable>
